#: of pyvista_wasm.camera.Camera.disable_parallel_projection:3
msgid ""
"Switches the camera from parallel projection to perspective projection. "
"This is equivalent to setting ``parallel_projection = False``."
msgstr ""

#: of pyvista_wasm.Camera.elevation:3
msgid ""
"The elevation angle controls the vertical rotation of the camera. It "
"rotates the camera about the cross product of the negative of the "
"direction of projection and the view up vector, using the focal point as "
"the center of rotation."
msgstr ""

#: of pyvista_wasm.Camera.elevation:8 pyvista_wasm.Camera.elevation:11
msgid "Elevation angle in degrees."
msgstr ""

#: of pyvista_wasm.camera.Camera.enable_parallel_projection:3
msgid ""
"Switches the camera from perspective projection to parallel projection. "
"This is equivalent to setting ``parallel_projection = True``."
msgstr ""

#: of pyvista_wasm.Camera.focal_point:3 pyvista_wasm.Camera.focal_point:6
msgid "Focal point as (x, y, z)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyvista_wasm.camera.Camera.orbit_elevation:3
msgid ""
"This method is named ``orbit_elevation`` to avoid conflict with the "
":attr:`elevation` property, which stores a static angle value."
msgstr ""

#: of pyvista_wasm.camera.Camera.orbit_elevation:6
msgid "Rotation angle in degrees.  Positive values tilt the camera upward."
msgstr ""

#: of pyvista_wasm.Camera.parallel_projection:3
msgid ""
"When True, uses parallel (orthographic) projection instead of perspective"
" projection. Parallel projection is useful for viewing 2D datasets, CAD-"
"like orthographic views, and scientific visualization where perspective "
"distortion is undesirable."
msgstr ""

#: of pyvista_wasm.Camera.parallel_projection:8
